REQP-1839#1 Warning
RAMB36 async control check  
The RAMB36E1 u_taxi_ethernet_subsystem/u_taxi_eth_mac_mii_fifo/tx_fifo/fifo_inst/mem_reg_0 has an input control pin u_taxi_ethernet_subsystem/u_taxi_eth_mac_mii_fifo/tx_fifo/fifo_inst/mem_reg_0/ENARDEN (net: u_taxi_ethernet_subsystem/u_taxi_eth_mac_mii_fifo/tx_fifo/fifo_inst/mem_reg_0_ENARDEN_cooolgate_en_sig_1) which is driven by a register (u_taxi_ethernet_subsystem/u_taxi_eth_mac_mii_fifo/tx_fifo/fifo_inst/s_reset_sync_inst/sync_reg_reg[3]) that has an active asychronous set or reset. This may cause corruption of the memory contents and/or read values when the set/reset is asserted and is not analyzed by the default static timing analysis. It is suggested to eliminate the use of a set/reset to registers driving this RAMB pin or else use a synchronous reset in which the assertion of the reset is timed by default.
Related violations: <none>

